  "problem": "In winter, the maximum daily temperature of a certain mountain location (rounded to the nearest degree) varies between $-{15}^{∘}C$ and ${2}^{∘}C,$ inclusive. Assuming that for a given winter day, each maximum temperature value between $-{15}^{∘}C$ and ${2}^{∘}C$ has an equal probability of occurring, what is the probability that the maximum daily temperature will reach at least ${0}^{∘}C$ on a randomly selected day?",
